  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "For a given value of \\(k,\\) the product of the roots of \\[ x^2-3kx+2k^2-1=0 \\] is \\(7.\\) The roots may be characterized as:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "integral and positive"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "integral and negative"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "rational, but not integral"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "irrational"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "imaginary"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "d",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1960-p11.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "By Vieta’s formulas, \\(2k^2-1=7,\\) so \\(k=\\pm2.\\) The roots are \\(3\\pm\\sqrt2\\) when \\(k=2,\\) and \\(-3\\pm\\sqrt2\\) when \\(k=-2.\\) In either case both roots are irrational.\n\nThus, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "Use the constant term to determine the possible values of \\(k\\)",
        "For either value of \\(k,\\) examine the quadratic formula or discriminant"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
